    {
      "id": "chat.composer_menu/v1",
      "key": "chat.composer_menu",
      "area": "chat/composer",
      "revision": 1,
      "label": "Entries of the + menu next to the message field (attach, model, tools, context, import)",
      "value": {
        "schema": "loom.composer_menu/1",
        "note": "Entries of the + menu next to the message field. label/reason name a word of presentation.ui_shell, or are {en, pl}. kind: attach (file picker), camera (photo: the camera on a phone, a picture file elsewhere), model (list of models; the choice is written to the conversation level of the scope chain under default_model, the key the kernel reads), submenu (items), toggle (on until turned off, a chip above the field says so: `field` + `value` = the request field it sets while on, e.g. web_search: true, deep_research: true, reasoning_effort: high, action: agent.run; or `flag` = a switch of this view: memory | knowledge), panel (opens a panel: import | graph | settings), unavailable (visible, with reason). exclusive: turning it on turns off the other field switches (an action takes only the words, no files). needs: settings that must not be empty, else the entry is unavailable with `reason` (and `panel` where they are set).",
        "items": [
          {
            "id": "attach_file",
            "label": "cm_attach_file",
            "kind": "attach"
          },
          {
            "id": "attach_photo",
            "label": "cm_attach_photo",
            "kind": "camera"
          },
          {
            "id": "model",
            "label": "cm_model",
            "kind": "model"
          },
          {
            "id": "tools",
            "label": "cm_tools",
            "kind": "submenu",
            "items": [
              {
                "id": "web_search",
                "label": "cm_web_search",
                "kind": "toggle",
                "field": "web_search",
                "value": true
              },
              {
                "id": "deep_research",
                "label": "cm_deep_research",
                "kind": "toggle",
                "field": "deep_research",
                "value": true
              },
              {
                "id": "thinking",
                "label": "cm_thinking",
                "kind": "toggle",
                "field": "reasoning_effort",
                "value": "high"
              },
              {
                "id": "agent",
                "label": "cm_agent",
                "kind": "toggle",
                "field": "action",
                "value": "agent.run",
                "exclusive": true
              },
              {
                "id": "image",
                "label": "cm_image",
                "kind": "toggle",
                "field": "action",
                "value": "depict",
                "exclusive": true,
                "needs": [
                  "image_model",
                  "image_provider"
                ],
                "reason": "cm_reason_image",
                "panel": "settings"
              },
              {
                "id": "music",
                "label": "cm_music",
                "kind": "unavailable",
                "reason": "cm_reason_music"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "context",
            "label": "cm_context",
            "kind": "submenu",
            "items": [
              {
                "id": "memory",
                "label": "cm_memory",
                "kind": "toggle",
                "flag": "memory"
              },
              {
                "id": "knowledge",
                "label": "cm_knowledge",
                "kind": "toggle",
                "flag": "knowledge"
              },
              {
                "id": "perspective",
                "label": "cm_perspective",
                "kind": "panel",
                "panel": "graph"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "import",
            "label": "cm_import",
            "kind": "panel",
            "panel": "import"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "chat.composer_menu_ops/v1",
      "key": "chat.composer_menu_ops",
      "area": "chat/composer",
      "revision": 1,
      "label": "Your own changes to the + menu: hide, add, reorder",
      "value": {
        "schema": "loom.composer_menu_ops/1",
        "note": "Your changes to the + menu, applied in order to the entries: {op: hide, id} | {op: add, item, parent?, before?} | {op: move, id, before?|parent?} . Empty = the menu as shipped.",
        "ops": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "presentation.graph_screen/v1",
      "key": "presentation.graph_screen",
      "area": "presentation/graph_screen",
      "revision": 1,
      "label": "Words of the graph navigator (Graph, Settings and You are views of one graph): the navigator, the honesty words (unknown with a reason, collapsed by the budget, hidden by you, no translation), the chips and evidence, the help per level of detail and the ROM note; texts only",
      "value": {
        "schema": "loom.presentation_feature/1",
        "feature": "graph_screen",
        "status": {
          "state": "present",
          "today": {
            "pl": "Lista i karta węzła są na ekranie (loom/web/src/components/GraphNavigator.tsx, NodeCard.tsx): menu ⋮ › Graf pokazuje wiersze korzenia z graph.navigate (etykieta, licznik albo „nieznane (powód)”, chip pochodzenia, po co), dotknięcie wiersza wchodzi głębiej, ścieżka cofa (także Wstecz Androida), lupa szuka na poziomie, Szerzej/Węziej i Głębiej/Płycej zmieniają budżet i głębię. Dotknięcie liścia albo ⋯ otwiera kartę z graph.card: wartość, po co, co zmienia, chip z warstwami, „Skąd jest wartość” całym łańcuchem (zwycięski poziom podświetlony, „bez projektu” jawnie), powiązania grupami, działania; Zmień → Dla kogo? → settings.set (Ty) / rules.set (rozmowa, projekt…) z potwierdzeniem, o które pyta silnik; „Zdejmij wartość: <warstwa>” przez rules.disable. Mapa, Perspektywa, Działania i Widok dojdą w kolejnych pakietach M1-W0 — ich przyciski mówią, że to planowane.",
            "en": "The list and the node card are on screen (loom/web/src/components/GraphNavigator.tsx, NodeCard.tsx): menu ⋮ › Graph shows the root rows from graph.navigate (label, count or “unknown (reason)”, provenance chip, what for), a tap on a row goes in, the path goes back (Android Back too), the magnifier searches on the level, Wider/Narrower and Deeper/Shallower change the budget and depth. A tap on a leaf or on ⋯ opens the card from graph.card: value, what for, what it changes, the chip with its layers, “Where the value comes from” as the whole chain (the winning level highlighted, “without a project” said), relations by kind, actions; Change → For whom? → settings.set (you) / rules.set (conversation, project …) with the confirmation the kernel asks for; “Take the value off: <layer>” through rules.disable. The map, Perspective, Actions and View come with the next packages of M1-W0 — their buttons say they are planned."
          },
          "reason": {
            "pl": "Słowa są w katalogu, żeby ekran nie wpisywał ich w kod; brak słowa pokazuje jego identyfikator.",
            "en": "The words are in the catalogue so the screen never writes them in code; a missing word shows its id."
          }
        },
